module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.InverseImageIdealSheaf
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.Localization
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.PushforwardCommutesCompletionConstructedIdeal
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Modules.LocalizationRingedSites.PullbackToposSquare

/-!
# `f^{-1}ℐ · 𝒪_X` localized: its restriction to a slice site and its globally generated form

Let `f : (Sh(𝒟), 𝒪') ⟶ (Sh(𝒞), 𝒪)` be a morphism of ringed sites, let `ℐ ⊂ 𝒪` be a sheaf of
ideals, let `V` be an object of the target site and put `U = u(V)`. Section 52.7 of the Stacks
Project takes the completion on the source along `ℐ' = f^{-1}ℐ · 𝒪_X`, which
`InverseImageIdealSheaf.lean` constructs as the image of the canonical map `f^*ℐ ⟶ 𝒪'`. This
file proves that that construction **commutes with restriction to a slice site**:

```
ℐ'|_U = (f')^{-1}(ℐ|_V) · 𝒪_U
```

for the localized morphism `f' : (Sh(𝒞/U), 𝒪_U) ⟶ (Sh(𝒟/V), 𝒪'_V)` of [Stacks, Tag 04J0]. This
is what makes the display of Section 52.7 a *local* question on the target site at the source's
own pair of sheaves of ideals: the restriction coherence of the comparison map
(`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCompletionPushforwardComparison_localized`) compares the
comparison map of `f` at `(ℐ, ℐ')` with that of `f'` at `(ℐ|_V, ℐ'|_U)`, and the identity proved
here says that the second sheaf of ideals of that pair is again the one Section 52.7 builds.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.overIdeal_inverseImageIdealSheaf`: **the identity above.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.over_inverseImageIdealMap`: the morphism-level statement it is
  deduced from — the canonical map `f^*ℐ ⟶ 𝒪'` restricted to `𝒞/U` is, through the localization
  square of [Stacks, Tag 04J0] and an automorphism of `𝒪_U`, the canonical map
  `(f')^*(ℐ|_V) ⟶ 𝒪_U` of the localized morphism.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.inverseImageIdealSheaf_generatedIdealSheaf`: **for an `ℐ`
  generated by finitely many global sections, `f^{-1}ℐ · 𝒪_X` is the ideal sheaf generated by
  the transported generators** — the identification of the general construction with the one
  `PushforwardCommutesCompletionConstructedIdeal.lean` makes. The two have the same universal
  property, so nothing about the sections of `f^*ℐ` is needed.

Together these two are what a local-to-global argument on the target site consumes: a covering
on whose members `ℐ` is globally generated gives, on each member, both sheaves of ideals in the
globally generated form in which the display of Section 52.7 is proved.

## Implementation notes

*Why an automorphism of `𝒪_U` appears, and why it is harmless.* The two halves of the
localization square that a consumer needs — the identification
`(f^*M)|_U ≅ (f')^*(M|_V)` of `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.Hom.localizedPullbackToposSquare`
and the comparison `(f')^*(𝒪'_V) ⟶ 𝒪_U` of `SheafOfModules.pullbackObjUnitToUnit` — are *not*
compatible on the nose, and cannot be made so: the square is assembled from
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.localizationPullbackToposIsoRestriction`, which is a
`Classical.choice` of an isomorphism between pullback along a localization morphism and
restriction to the slice site ([Stacks, Tag 04IX]), so no equation whose two sides differ by an
automorphism of the structure sheaf can be proved about it. Two such choices enter the square,
one on each site, and nothing cancels them.

Nothing is lost, because the statement wanted here is about an **image**, and the image of a map
into `𝒪_U` does not change when the map is composed with an automorphism of `𝒪_U`: such an
automorphism is multiplication by a global section which is a unit, and a sheaf of ideals is
carried onto itself by it. That is
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule_comp_unitIso`, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.localizedUnitDiscrepancy` names the automorphism by which the two
identifications of `(f^*𝒪)|_U` with `𝒪_U` differ. So the only input about the square is its
**naturality**, which is free, together with the invertibility of the two comparison maps
`f^*𝒪 ⟶ 𝒪'` and `(f')^*𝒪'_V ⟶ 𝒪_U`, which is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_pullbackObjUnitToUnit_fSharpRing` at `f` and at `f'`.

*Why the proofs are written in term mode.* Both spellings of the sheaf of rings on the slice site
occur — `((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).over U`, in which restriction to the slice
site and `overIdeal` are stated, and `(Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (X.over U).O)`, in
which the localized morphism of ringed sites and its comparison map are — and they are
definitionally equal but not syntactically so. The statements below therefore mix them and are
type-correct only at default transparency, which is enough for `exact`, `refine` and the `trans`
tactic and not enough for `rw`.

Deliberately untagged: this is a property of the construction of Section 52.7, not a statement of
the Stacks Project. [Stacks, Tag 04J0] is registered on
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.Hom.localized` and on the squares of
`StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/Sites/Modules/LocalizationRingedSites/PullbackToposSquare.lean`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 04IX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04IX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 04J0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04J0)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0G](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0G)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0I](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0I)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite
open AlgebraicGeometry

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

attribute [local instance] AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.hasSheafCompose_forget₂_ringCat

variable {X Y : RingedSite.{u, u, u}}
  [HasWeakSheafify X.J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [X.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ U : X.C, HasWeakSheafify (X.J.over U) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ U : X.C, (X.J.over U).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ W : Y.C, HasWeakSheafify (Y.J.over W) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ W : Y.C, (Y.J.over W).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  (f : RingedSite.Hom X Y)
  (I : SheafOfModules.Submodule
    (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O))))
  (V : Y.C)

/-- The restriction to `𝒞/U` of the comparison map `f^*𝒪 ⟶ 𝒪'`, with its target read in the
spelling `𝒪_U = (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (X.over U).O)` that the localized morphism
of ringed sites uses. -/
def overPullbackObjUnitToUnit :
    (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) (f.u.obj V)).obj
        (f.toRingedToposSiteHom.pullbackTopos.obj
          (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)))) ≅
      SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (X.over (f.u.obj V)).O)) :=
  (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) (f.u.obj V)).mapIso
    (@asIso _ _ _ _ _ (isIso_pullbackObjUnitToUnit_fSharpRing f))

/-- **The automorphism of `𝒪_U` by which the two identifications of `(f^*𝒪)|_U` with `𝒪_U`
differ.** One is the restriction to `𝒞/U` of the comparison map `f^*𝒪 ⟶ 𝒪'`; the other is the
localization square of [Stacks, Tag 04J0] at `𝒪` followed by the comparison map
`(f')^*(𝒪'_V) ⟶ 𝒪_U` of the localized morphism. Both are invertible, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_pullbackObjUnitToUnit_fSharpRing` at `f` and at `f'`, so they
differ by an automorphism of `𝒪_U`, which is what this is.

It is not the identity, and nothing says it should be: the localization square is assembled from
a `Classical.choice` of the isomorphism of [Stacks, Tag 04IX] on each of the two sites. Every
statement below is insensitive to it, by
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule_comp_unitIso`. -/
def localizedUnitDiscrepancy :
    SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (X.over (f.u.obj V)).O)) ≅
      SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (X.over (f.u.obj V)).O)) :=
  (@asIso _ _ _ _ _ (isIso_pullbackObjUnitToUnit_fSharpRing (f.localized V))).symm ≪≫
    ((f.localizedPullbackToposSquare V).app
      (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)))).symm ≪≫
    overPullbackObjUnitToUnit f V

/-- Inserting an isomorphism and its inverse after `a`: `a ≫ k = (a ≫ e.hom) ≫ e.inv ≫ k`. -/
private theorem comp_eq_comp_hom_comp_inv_comp {C : Type*} [Category C] {A B D E : C}
    (a : A ⟶ B) (e : B ≅ D) (k : B ⟶ E) : a ≫ k = (a ≫ e.hom) ≫ e.inv ≫ k := by
  simp

/-- **The canonical map `f^*ℐ ⟶ 𝒪'` of Section 52.7 restricted to a slice site is the canonical
map of the localized morphism**, through the localization square of [Stacks, Tag 04J0] at `ℐ`
and the automorphism `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.localizedUnitDiscrepancy` of `𝒪_U`.

The square is used only through its naturality at the inclusion `ℐ ↪ 𝒪`: the restriction of
`f^*(ℐ ↪ 𝒪)` is, up to the square at `ℐ` and at `𝒪`, the pullback along `f'` of the inclusion
`ℐ|_V ↪ 𝒪'_V`. What remains is the comparison of the two maps into `𝒪_U`, which is the
definition of the discrepancy. -/
theorem over_inverseImageIdealMap :
    (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) (f.u.obj V)).map
        (inverseImageIdealMap f I) =
      ((f.localizedPullbackToposSquare V).app I.toSheafOfModules).hom ≫
        inverseImageIdealMap (f.localized V) (overIdeal I V) ≫
          (localizedUnitDiscrepancy f V).hom := by
  trans
      (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))
        (f.u.obj V)).map
        (f.toRingedToposSiteHom.pullbackTopos.map I.ι) ≫
      (overPullbackObjUnitToUnit f V).hom
  · exact
      (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))
        (f.u.obj V)).map_comp _ _
  trans (((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))
          (f.u.obj V)).map
          (f.toRingedToposSiteHom.pullbackTopos.map I.ι) ≫
        ((f.localizedPullbackToposSquare V).app
          (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)))).hom) ≫
      ((f.localizedPullbackToposSquare V).app
          (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)))).inv ≫
        (overPullbackObjUnitToUnit f V).hom)
  · exact comp_eq_comp_hom_comp_inv_comp _ _ _
  trans ((((f.localizedPullbackToposSquare V).app I.toSheafOfModules).hom ≫
        (f.localized V).toRingedToposSiteHom.pullbackTopos.map
          ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)) V).map
            I.ι)) ≫
      ((f.localizedPullbackToposSquare V).app
          (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)))).inv ≫
        (overPullbackObjUnitToUnit f V).hom)
  · exact congrArg (fun m => m ≫ _) ((f.localizedPullbackToposSquare V).hom.naturality I.ι)
  refine (Category.assoc _ _ _).trans (congrArg (fun m => _ ≫ m) ?_)
  exact comp_eq_comp_hom_comp_inv_comp _ (@asIso _ _ _ _ _
    (isIso_pullbackObjUnitToUnit_fSharpRing (f.localized V))) _

/-- **`ℐ' = f^{-1}ℐ · 𝒪_X` restricts to the ideal sheaf of the same name for the localized
morphism**: `ℐ'|_U = (f')^{-1}(ℐ|_V) · 𝒪_U`, where `U = u(V)` and `f'` is the localized morphism
of [Stacks, Tag 04J0].

The image subsheaf commutes with restriction to a slice site
(`Stacks.SheafOfModules.ImageSubsheaf.over_imageSubmodule`), so the left-hand side is the image
of the restricted canonical map; that map is the canonical map of `f'` precomposed with an
isomorphism and postcomposed with an automorphism of `𝒪_U`, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.over_inverseImageIdealMap`, and neither changes the image, by
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule_iso_hom_comp` and
`.imageSubmodule_comp_unitIso`.

Note that the statement is **false** for a sheaf of ideals satisfying only the relation
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.PushforwardIdealCompatible` of [Stacks, Tag 099J] — take
`ℐ' = 𝒪'`, whose restriction is `𝒪_U` — so it is a property of the construction and not of the
relation. -/
theorem overIdeal_inverseImageIdealSheaf :
    overIdeal (inverseImageIdealSheaf f I) (f.u.obj V) =
      inverseImageIdealSheaf (f.localized V) (overIdeal I V) := by
  refine Eq.trans
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.ImageSubsheaf.over_imageSubmodule (inverseImageIdealMap f I)
      (f.u.obj V)) ?_
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg (fun m => Stacks.SheafOfModules.ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule m)
    (over_inverseImageIdealMap f I V)) ?_
  exact (Stacks.SheafOfModules.ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule_iso_hom_comp _ _).trans
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule_comp_unitIso _
      (localizedUnitDiscrepancy f V))

/-! ### The globally generated case -/

section Generated

variable (g : RingedSite.Hom X Y) {T : Y.C} (hT : IsTerminal T) (hT' : IsTerminal (g.u.obj T))
  {s : ℕ} (t : Fin s → Presheaf.globalSections (Y.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u}))

omit [∀ U : X.C, HasWeakSheafify (X.J.over U) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ U : X.C, (X.J.over U).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ W : Y.C, HasWeakSheafify (Y.J.over W) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ W : Y.C, (Y.J.over W).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}] in
include hT in
/-- **At a sheaf of ideals generated by finitely many global sections, `f^{-1}ℐ · 𝒪_X` is the
ideal sheaf generated by the transported generators**: for `ℐ = (t_1, …, t_s)`,
`f^{-1}ℐ · 𝒪_X = (f^♯t_1, …, f^♯t_s)`.

This is `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.eq_generatedIdealSheaf_pushGlobalSections`, which
characterises the ideal sheaf generated by the transported generators as the least one receiving
`f^♯(f^{-1}ℐ)`, fed the two halves of that characterisation for the image construction:
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.pushforwardIdealCompatible_inverseImageIdealSheaf` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.inverseImageIdealSheaf_le`.

The implementation notes of `InverseImageIdealSheaf.lean` used to record this identification as
unavailable, on the ground that it would need `f^*ℐ` to be generated by the pulled-back
generators. It does not: the two constructions have the same universal property, and that is
enough. -/
theorem inverseImageIdealSheaf_generatedIdealSheaf :
    inverseImageIdealSheaf g (generatedIdealSheaf t) =
      generatedIdealSheaf (pushGlobalSections g hT' t) :=
  eq_generatedIdealSheaf_pushGlobalSections g hT hT' t
    (pushforwardIdealCompatible_inverseImageIdealSheaf g (generatedIdealSheaf t))
    fun _ h => inverseImageIdealSheaf_le g (generatedIdealSheaf t) _ h

end Generated

end AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

end
